From: Tyler Baker <tyler@foundries.io>
Date: Mon, 26 May 2026
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: arduino-imola: disable anx7625

Holding fix for a runtime crash on UNO Q (QRB2210 / arduino-imola) running
linux-qcom-next 7.1-rc4. The anx7625 MIPI-DSI -> DP altmode bridge driver
NULL-derefs in drm_atomic_state_alloc during probe:

  Unable to handle kernel read from unreadable memory at virtual address 0x338
  pc : drm_atomic_state_alloc+0xc/0x78 [drm]
  lr : drm_self_refresh_helper_entry_work+0x58/0x1e0 [drm_kms_helper]

A workqueue runs drm_self_refresh against a drm_atomic_state that doesn't
exist because the DRM stack got torn down mid-probe. The kernel taints W
and continues, but userspace never reaches multi-user.target -- rmtfs and
tqftpserv never start, the wcn3990 firmware never loads, wlan0 never comes
up, no SSH path.

Disabling the bridge in DT keeps the DRM stack out of the failing init
path. The MSM DRM driver still probes DSI panels and finds nothing to
drive (harmless WARN_ONs), but the rest of userspace proceeds.
Trade-off: no DP altmode on USB-C (no external display over Type-C)
until the upstream probe-order issue is fixed.

Drop this patch when the upstream anx7625 probe-order issue is fixed
(currently being worked on dri-devel; thread closest in shape is the
PD-detect rework at lkml.org/lkml/2026/2/12/230, though the crash
signature here is different).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [holding fix; not posted upstream]
Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler@foundries.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola.dts
@@ -246,6 +246,7 @@
 	status = "okay";

 	anx7625: encoder@58 {
+		status = "disabled";
 		compatible = "analogix,anx7625";
 		reg = <0x58>;
 		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 81 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;
